{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "list_id": "medicine-2026",
  "run": 1,
  "simulation_id": "sim-40",
  "member_id": "svenningsson-per",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/medicine_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B003",
        "laureates": [
          "Jens Juul Holst",
          "Svetlana Mojsov",
          "Daniel J. Drucker"
        ],
        "citation": "for discoveries of GLP-1 physiology that enabled transformative therapies for diabetes and obesity"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B002",
    "B001"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B003 remains the strongest unified case for a foundational physiological discovery, a clearly causal therapeutic translation, and mature benefit at exceptional scale in diabetes and obesity. The citation deliberately recognizes GLP-1 physiology and what it enabled, rather than assigning the entire subsequent medicinal-development enterprise to three individuals. Within that delimited achievement, Holst, Mojsov, and Drucker remain the most coherent allocation across physiological discovery, molecular characterization, and translational understanding.",
    "case_against": "The credit boundary remains the principal weakness. Later durable-therapeutic development includes substantial contributions outside the proposed trio, including Lotte Bjerre Knudsen, so an imprecise citation would overstate what this allocation represents. B002 offers a more tractable account of three essential contributors and B001 offers an especially focused mechanism-to-treatment narrative; both therefore remain serious alternatives.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "perlmann-thomas",
        "point": "Perlmann gives B002 narrow priority because the Clark-Hochmair-Wilson configuration may more cleanly delimit essential implant and speech-processing advances than the GLP-1 achievement can delimit physiology from later drug development.",
        "response": "This is a substantial comparative advantage for B002, and its decades of restored speech perception are mature and transformative. I retain B003 because a tightly physiology-centered citation and the Holst-Mojsov-Drucker allocation identify a defensible scientific core without claiming all later pharmaceutical development. On the supplied evidence, the resulting link from basic physiology to broad, established treatment in two major diseases outweighs B002's relative attribution advantage."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "linnarsson-sten",
        "point": "Linnarsson prioritizes B036 for its durable prevention of HPV infection and HPV-related cancers, while requiring separation of the virus-like-particle vaccine advance from earlier recognition of HPV causation.",
        "response": "B036 remains an outstanding alternative, particularly for prevention and population-level medical benefit. The needed distinction from prior HPV-causation recognition and the broader pathway of vaccine development remain material attribution questions on the supplied record. B003 also requires careful delimitation, but its proposed citation can specifically confine recognition to GLP-1 physiology and its therapeutic consequences, leaving the preferred configuration more clearly bounded at this stage."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "wahren-herlenius-marie",
        "point": "Wahren-Herlenius agrees that B003's citation must stay centered on foundational GLP-1 physiology and not imply that three laureates created all subsequent therapies.",
        "response": "I agree. This delimitation is the condition for retaining the configuration: it makes the cited discovery, rather than the full industrial and clinical history of individual medicines, the object of recognition. It also explains why the configuration remains unchanged despite the legitimate claim of later therapeutic-development contributors."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the supplied evidence can ultimately support the Holst-Mojsov-Drucker allocation as sufficiently complete for the narrowly framed GLP-1 physiological achievement.",
      "Whether B002's foundational implant and processing advances can be separated more sharply from later technical, surgical, and programming refinements than is presently documented.",
      "Whether B036 can be delimited from earlier HPV-causation recognition and its wider translational pathway with enough precision for the proposed allocation."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No candidate-specific conflict is apparent from the supplied profile. I disclose that the profile records approximately twenty co-authored works with Thomas Perlmann, an unaudited OpenAlex count that may be inflated; this is not a documented connection to any preferred or alternative candidate."
  }
}
